    "title": "How to live stream Miami (OH) vs SMU: March Madness First Four, TV channel",
    "text": "Miami (OH) faces SMU in a First Four matchup of the 2026 NCAA Tournament on Wednesday as March Madness officially gets underway. MORE: Predicting upsets in March Madness 2026 Mar 11, 2026; Charlotte, NC, USA; Southern Methodist University Mustangs center Jaden Toombs (10) with the ball in the first half at Spectrum Center. Mandatory Credit: Bob Donnan-Imagn Image How to Watch Miami (OH) vs SMU Date: Wednesday, March 18, 2026 Time: 9:15 PM ET TV Channel: truTV Live Stream: DIRECTV (try for free); Sling (watch now) The NCAA Tournament tips off with 68 teams chasing college basketball’s biggest prize, setting the stage for three weeks of upsets, buzzer-beaters, and dramatic finishes. As all the top teams in the nation have their eyes set on a national championship, the tournament once again promises the chaos and excitement that make March Madness one of the most thrilling events in sports. – Watch every NCAA Tournament matchup on DIRECTV – The Miami (OH) RedHawks enter the NCAA Tournament with a 31–1 overall record, going 18–0 in Mid‑American Conference (MAC) play to capture the MAC regular‑season title before falling in the conference tournament quarterfinals. The season marks a historic performance for Miami, its first NCAA bid since 2007 and its first at‑large selection ever, and the RedHawks are seeded No. 11 in the Midwest Region, opening tournament play in the First Four in Dayton. Their opponent, the SMU Mustangs, earned an at‑large bid with a 20–13 record and an 8–10 mark in Atlantic Coast Conference (ACC) play, finishing in the middle of the ACC standings before a second‑round exit in the ACC Tournament. SMU also carries an 11 seed in the Midwest Region and will aim to use its experience and league schedule strength to knock off Miami (OH) and advance to face No. 6 Tennessee in the Round of 64. Live stream Miami (OH) vs SMU with DIRECTV: Start your free trial now! Live stream Miami (OH) vs SMU with Sling: Start your subscription now! Fans can watch every moment of the NCAA Tournament through streaming platforms like DIRECTV and Sling as March Madness gets underway. Games throughout the tournament are broadcast on CBS, TBS, TNT, and truTV, with DIRECTV packages providing access to all four networks, so viewers can stream every round live. Sling also offers coverage of much of the tournament through its packages that include TBS, TNT, and truTV. Regional restrictions may apply. If you purchase a product or register for an account through one of the links on our site, we may receive compensation. — Enjoy free coverage of the top news & trending stories on The Big Lead — MARCH MADNESS: 5 bold March Madness predictions for 2026 NCAA Tournament NFL DRAFT: New Mel Kiper NFL mock draft shows major impact of free agency MLB: Dodgers announce Shohei Ohtani’s spring training pitching debut NHL: Oilers’ Leon Draisaitl out for regular season with lower-body injury ENTERTAINMENT: Is ‘Bachelorette’ still airing amid Taylor Frankie Paul domestic dispute allegations? VIRAL: Livvy Dunne shares ‘Baywatch’ training with BTS swimsuit, set photos",
